2. The Reasoned Schemer, first edition

   Files:   miniKanren/amb/trs1/main.rkt

   Source:  Daniel P. Friedman, William E. Byrd, and Oleg Kiselyov,
            The Reasoned Schemer, MIT Press, 2005, appendix A
            ("Connecting the Wires").

   Copyright (C) 2005 Massachusetts Institute of Technology.

   The user-level language (run, fresh, all/alli, conde/condi/conda/
   condu, project) follows the book, and the cond-aux and all-aux macros
   keep the structure of the book's implementation.  The remaining
   definitions are rewritten on top of amb.


3. The Reasoned Schemer, second edition

   Files:   miniKanren/amb/trs2/main.rkt

   Source:  https://github.com/TheReasonedSchemer2ndEd/CodeFromTheReasonedSchemer2ndEd
            (trs2-impl.scm), the code of chapter 10 and appendix A of
            Daniel P. Friedman, William E. Byrd, Oleg Kiselyov, and
            Jason Hemann, The Reasoned Schemer, second edition, MIT
            Press, 2018.

   The user-level language (run, run*, defrel, fresh, conde, conda,
   condu, project, disj, conj) and the definitions of walk, unify,
   ifte, once, and reification follow that code.  Goals are rewritten
   on top of amb, without streams: disj2 is a choice made by amb,
   conj2 is function composition, and the suspension that defrel
   inserts is a choice point sent to the back of amb's frontier.  The
